Fix: "BaseHeap::Release failed because address is not a region start" (race in PhysicalHeap::Release)

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0008-physical-release-order.patch
Status:     local patch, not upstream yet (same code in Xenia: worth reporting)

WHAT BROKE
  Physical memory (the 0xA0000000 / 0xC0000000 / 0xE0000000 windows) is
  bookkept twice: once in the shared "parent" heap of physical pages, once
  in the window's own page table. PhysicalHeap::Release freed the PARENT
  pages first and the window's entry second, with the global lock dropped
  in between (TriggerCallbacks takes it by value). PhysicalHeap::Alloc on
  another thread could land in that gap: the parent handed it the pages that
  had just been freed, and BaseHeap::AllocFixed pinned them in the window
  on top of the old, not-yet-released entry (a reserve+commit request is
  allowed over reserved pages). The first thread's BaseHeap::Release then
  wiped the entry, which by now belonged to the NEW allocation. When that
  allocation was freed later, the window had no record of it: "address is
  not a region start" (the physical pages were still freed, so no leak, but
  in between the window's bookkeeping lied about memory that was in use:
  anything asking the page table, e.g. a readability check, saw it as free).

HOW WE FOUND IT (2026-09-30)
  Crash: Mind over Mutant logged 1-7 of these errors per play session, on
  the main thread, when a new part of a level streamed in or when quitting
  a level to the menu. A temporary diagnostic (freed address, the window's
  page entry, guest call stacks, plus a history of every physical alloc and
  free keyed by physical address) showed, for every failing address: D3D
  created a texture there (XMemAlloc -> XPhysicalAlloc), and the very next
  release in the history was the XMA audio library (0x8247D730) freeing its
  OWN old buffer at that same address on another thread; the texture's
  destroy (0x823069BC/C8, D3D resource release -> XMemFree) then failed.
  Reproduced by loading a Ratcicle Kingdom save and quitting to the menu (6
  errors, all texture base / mip addresses, all with that pattern).

THE FIX
  Invalidate (callbacks) while the region is still whole, release the
  window's own entry FIRST, then the parent's pages. While the parent still
  holds the pages, no Alloc can be given them, so there's no gap left. As a
  side effect a free of an address the window doesn't know is refused
  before it can release parent pages that might belong to someone else.
  out_region_size still reports the parent's size, as before.

diff --git a/src/system/xmemory.cpp b/src/system/xmemory.cpp
index 76cc877..6643479 100644
--- a/src/system/xmemory.cpp
+++ b/src/system/xmemory.cpp
@@ -2023,10 +2023,6 @@ bool PhysicalHeap::Release(uint32_t base_address, uint32_t* out_region_size) {
   auto global_lock = global_critical_region_.Acquire();
 
   uint32_t parent_base_address = GetPhysicalAddress(base_address);
-  if (!parent_heap_->Release(parent_base_address, out_region_size)) {
-    REXSYS_ERROR("PhysicalHeap::Release failed due to parent heap failure");
-    return false;
-  }
 
   // Must invalidate here because the range being released may be reused in
   // another mapping of physical memory - but callback flags are set in each
@@ -2036,12 +2032,30 @@ bool PhysicalHeap::Release(uint32_t base_address, uint32_t* out_region_size) {
   // state of the allocator as of February 24th, 2020). If memory is invalidated
   // in Alloc instead, Alloc won't be aware of callbacks enabled in other heaps,
   // thus callback handlers will keep considering this range valid forever.
+  // Done while the region is still whole (the callbacks read its protection),
+  // and before the physical pages can go to anyone else.
   uint32_t region_size;
   if (QuerySize(base_address, &region_size)) {
     TriggerCallbacks(std::move(global_lock), base_address, region_size, true, true);
   }
 
-  return BaseHeap::Release(base_address, out_region_size);
+  // Release THIS view's pages first, the parent (physical) pages second. The
+  // old order (parent first) left a window in which another thread's Alloc got
+  // the same physical pages from the parent and pinned them here on top of our
+  // not-yet-released entry (AllocFixed accepts a commit over reserved pages);
+  // our BaseHeap::Release then wiped the NEW owner's entry, and its own free
+  // later failed with "address is not a region start". While the parent still
+  // holds the pages nobody can be handed them, so this order has no window.
+  // Bonus: a free of an address this view doesn't know no longer releases
+  // physical pages that may belong to someone else.
+  if (!BaseHeap::Release(base_address, nullptr)) {
+    return false;
+  }
+  if (!parent_heap_->Release(parent_base_address, out_region_size)) {
+    REXSYS_ERROR("PhysicalHeap::Release failed due to parent heap failure");
+    return false;
+  }
+  return true;
 }
 
 bool PhysicalHeap::Protect(uint32_t address, uint32_t size, uint32_t protect,
